<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#vietnamese-alphabet">Glossary</a> · Term · script</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vietnamese alphabet</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as chữ Quốc ngữ, Quốc ngữ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vietnamese alphabet, chữ Quốc ngữ, is the Latin-based script used to write Vietnamese, with diacritics marking tones and vowels. Developed by Portuguese and French Catholic missionaries in the 17th century, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-de-rhodes">Alexandre de Rhodes</a>, it was promoted under French rule and became the national writing system in the 20th century, replacing classical Chinese and chữ Nôm.</p></div>
